          { "kind": "rem", "text": "val infiniteTransition = rememberInfiniteTransition(label = \"gradientTransition\")" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "val angle by infiniteTransition.animateFloat(initialValue = 0f, targetValue = 360f, ...)" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "val onPaletteExtracted: (Color, Color) -> Unit = { dominant, vibrant -> ... }" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "DisposableEffect(article.itemId) { onDispose { dominantColor = Color.Transparent; ... } }" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "val parsedSnippet: AnnotatedString? = if (!article.snippet.isNullOrBlank()) { HtmlCompat.fromHtml(...) } else null" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "val parsedSnippet: AnnotatedString? = remember(article.snippet) {" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "    if (!article.snippet.isNullOrBlank()) HtmlCompat.fromHtml(article.snippet, HtmlCompat.FROM_HTML_MODE_LEGACY).toSpannable().toAnnotatedString(colorScheme.onSurface) else null" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "}" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "val tagStates = remember(article.itemId) { mutableStateMapOf<String, Boolean>() }" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "LaunchedEffect(article.tagsString) { /* sync tags */ }" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "LaunchedEffect(article.itemId, tags) { /* add missing tags */ }" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "val tagStates: Map<String, Boolean> = remember(article.tagsString, tags) {" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "    buildMap { tags.forEach { put(it, false) }; article.tags.forEach { put(it, true) } }" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "}" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>ArticleThumbnail.kt — drop palette, gradient overlay, and allowHardware(false)</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Remove <code>dominantColor</code>, <code>vibrantColor</code>, <code>onPaletteExtracted</code> params. Delete the conditional gradient overlay <code>Box</code> (lines 54–68). Remove <code>allowHardware(false)</code> from the <code>ImageRequest</code> so display images decode as hardware-backed bitmaps. Remove the <code>.listener(onSuccess)</code> palette-extraction call. Replace the <code>vibrantColor.copy(alpha=0.6f)</code> shadow tint with <code>Color.Black.copy(alpha=0.08f)</code>.</p>
